abstract: >-
  Replication package for the paper. Walk-forward analysis removes rule-level data snooping but has
  design settings of its own (training-window type and length, test-block length, gap). The package
  measures the false-positive rate of choosing among 56 walk-forward designs by Monte Carlo, reports the
  dependence between designs, and provides bootstrap tests across designs, with an illustration on a
  century of US market returns and five regional indices.
